# {{.Slug}}

A static blog exported by [Open Prose](https://github.com/anthropics/open-prose). Built on Next.js 16 + MDX. Everything in this folder is yours — there's no build step that depends on the editor, and no runtime that calls home.

## Run locally

```bash
npm install
npm run dev
```

Open http://localhost:3000.

## Deploy

This is a regular Next.js app. Pick whichever host you like:

- **Vercel** — `vercel deploy` (or push to a connected GitHub repo). One click; image optimization works out of the box.
- **Netlify** — set the build command to `npm run build` and leave the publish directory blank. The Netlify Next.js adapter handles routing.
- **Cloudflare Pages** — same as Netlify; pick the Next.js framework preset and Cloudflare wires it up.
- **Any Node host** — `npm run build && npm start` runs the production server on port 3000.

### Static export (no Node needed)

If you want a fully static site for GitHub Pages, S3, or similar:

```js
// next.config.mjs
const nextConfig = {
  output: "export",
  images: { unoptimized: true },
  // ...
};
```

Run `npm run build`, then deploy the `out/` folder. **Tradeoff**: `next/image` becomes a pass-through — no AVIF/WebP conversion, no responsive `srcset`, no resizing. Drop pre-sized images into `public/` and serve them at one resolution.

## Add images

Drop files into `public/media/` and reference them as `/media/foo.jpg`. The Open Prose editor uploads here automatically; manual edits land here too.

For inline body images, use standard markdown — they render as lazy-loaded `<img>` tags:

```md
![A short description](/media/foo.jpg)
```

For hero or large images where you know the dimensions, use `<Image>` directly in MDX. This gets you AVIF, WebP, responsive `srcset`, and zero layout shift:

```mdx
<Image
  src="/media/hero.jpg"
  alt="A short description"
  width={1200}
  height={630}
  sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 720px"
/>
```

The `sizes` hint is the only knob that controls which `srcset` candidate the browser picks. Match it to where the image actually appears on the page (`100vw` for full-bleed, `720px` for a centered prose column, etc.).

## Edit content

- **Posts** — `content/posts/*.mdx`. Frontmatter at the top (title, slug, date, tags, description, coverImage), MDX body below.
- **Home page** — `content/home.mdx`. Optional. Renders inside the home page above the recent-posts list.
- **About page** — `content/about.mdx`. Optional. Becomes `/about`.
- **Site config** — `src/lib/site.ts`. Name, author, URL, social links, navigation, header tagline, footer copyright.

## Edit design

- **Colors, fonts, radii** — top of `src/styles/globals.css`. CSS custom properties with sensible defaults.
- **Per-template prose styles** — same file, the `.prose-{template}` block. Margins, headings, code blocks, tables, images, the lot.
- **Header / Footer markup** — `src/components/Header.tsx`, `src/components/Footer.tsx`.
- **Page layouts** — `src/app/page.tsx`, `src/app/blog/page.tsx`, `src/app/blog/[slug]/page.tsx`, `src/app/about/page.tsx`.

## What's already optimized

- **`next/image`** with AVIF + WebP, responsive `srcset`, lazy loading by default. Cover images load with `priority` so they don't lazy.
- **`next/font/google`** self-hosts the typefaces — no third-party request, automatic preload, automatic `size-adjust` to neutralize CLS during fallback.
- **Static metadata** — every route generates `<title>`, OG tags, Twitter card tags from frontmatter and site config.
- **`sitemap.xml`**, **`robots.txt`**, **RSS feed** at `/feed.xml`.
- **JSON-LD structured data** — Article, BlogPosting, WebSite, Organization, BreadcrumbList, ProfilePage. Helps Google understand the content.
- **`sharp`** for fast image transformation in production builds.

## Where things live

- `content/posts/*.mdx` — your blog posts.
- `content/home.mdx` — home page body (optional).
- `content/about.mdx` — about page body (optional).
- `public/media/` — uploaded images and other assets.
- `src/lib/site.ts` — site config.
- `src/lib/content.ts` — reads posts and pages from disk with frontmatter.
- `src/lib/seo.ts` — JSON-LD graph builders.
- `src/app/layout.tsx` — root layout, metadata, fonts.
- `src/app/page.tsx` — home page.
- `src/app/blog/page.tsx` — blog index.
- `src/app/blog/[slug]/page.tsx` — single post.
- `src/app/about/page.tsx` — about page.
- `src/app/sitemap.ts` — sitemap.xml.
- `src/app/robots.ts` — robots.txt.
- `src/app/feed.xml/route.ts` — RSS feed.
- `src/styles/globals.css` — tokens + per-template prose.
- `src/components/Header.tsx`, `Footer.tsx`, `MobileNav.tsx`.
- `mdx-components.tsx` — element overrides for MDX (`<img>`, `<Image>`, links, tables, code).
- `next.config.mjs` — image optimization knobs and Next.js config.

